# ============================================================
# .gitignore — ANN From Scratch: MNIST Digit Recognizer
# ============================================================
#
# DEPLOYMENT NOTE: Render and Streamlit Cloud have no training step in
# this repo's deploy pipeline -- the live API/dashboard just loads
# whatever champion model is already committed. That means ann_models/
# (weights + registry + model cards) and the sample dataset are
# INTENTIONALLY tracked by git, not ignored. Only the full ~40k-row
# Kaggle CSV (too large, and re-downloadable) and regenerable runtime
# junk are excluded below.
# ============================================================

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Test / coverage artifacts (regenerate on every test run) ──
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ── Jupyter ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Virtual environments ────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── OS junk ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# ── Full Kaggle dataset — NOT pushed ────────────────────────
# ~70MB+, re-downloadable from Kaggle (see README Quickstart step 2).
# The small balanced sample (data/sample_train.csv, ~300 rows) and the
# demo image (data/sample_digit.png) ARE committed -- they're small
# and needed for anyone cloning the repo to test/demo without Kaggle.
data/train.csv
data/test.csv
!data/sample_dataset_info.txt
!data/sample_digit.png
!data/sample_mnist_train.csv

# ── Runtime-generated prediction logs ───────────────────────
# Regenerated automatically by every API call / simulation run --
# not meaningful in version control, would just cause merge noise.
!logs/*.csv
!logs/.gitkeep

# ── Simulator monitoring artifacts ──────────────────────────
# monitor_scores.csv / feature_drift_report.csv are regenerated by
# scripts/run_simulation.py -- not committed so a fresh clone shows a
# clean dashboard until the new owner runs their own simulation.
!ann_models/monitor_scores.csv
!ann_models/feature_drift_report.csv

# ── Env / secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
*.pem
*.key

# NOTE: everything else under ann_models/ (*.npz weights,
# latest_model.json, model_card_*.json, challenger_log.json) and
# data/sample_train.csv, data/sample_digit.png are DELIBERATELY left
# trackable -- Render and Streamlit Cloud need them at deploy time.